How do we know whether our machine learning model is actually good?
A model may perform very well on the data it learned from but fail when it receives new data. Today, you'll learn how to identify this problem and evaluate models correctly.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
|What is model evaluation?|

Model evaluation is the process of measuring how well a trained model makes predictions on data.

Imagine a banking application that predicts loan defaults.
- Training accuracy: 99%
- Test accuracy: 65%

Is this a good model? Probably not. The large difference suggests the model may have memorized the training data instead of learning patterns that generalize.
A model should perform well on unseen data, not just training data.
